„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections—…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦And it came to pass, when he had made an end of speaking unto Saul, that the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd Saul took him that day, and would let him go no more home to his father's house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNThen Jonathan and David made a covenant, because he loved him as his own soul.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšAnd Jonathan stripped himself of the robe that was upon him, and gave it to David, and his garments, even to his sword, and to his bow, and to his girdle.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÏAnd David went out whithersoever Saul sent him, and behaved himself wisely: and Saul set him over the men of war, and he was accepted in the sight of all the people, and also in the sight of Saul's servants.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙğAnd it came to pass as they came, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, that the women came out of all cities of Israel, singing and dancing, to meet king Saul, with tabrets, with joy, and with instruments of musick.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ<And the women answered one another as they played, and said,¦layout ‚¤text¾Saul hath slain his thousands,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼And David his ten thousands.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈAnd Saul was very wroth, and the saying displeased him; and he said, They have ascribed unto David ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed but thousands: and what can he have more but the kingdom?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.And Saul eyed David from that day and forward.¦